# Known-harness fatal-diagnostic allowlist for scripts/run-gd-tests.sh running
# council's suites. One extended-regex pattern per line, matched against
# composite records of the form
#
#     <diagnostic line> @@ <its `at:` location line>
#
# Every `SCRIPT ERROR:` and `ERROR: Failed to load script` record that matches
# NO pattern here FAILS the suite that printed it, even when its Results line is
# green. So each entry is a claim — "this diagnostic is the HOST HARNESS's, not
# the suite's" — and each needs its proof written next to it. A pattern added to
# silence a red run is the same act as deleting the assertion that failed.
#
# COUNCIL ALLOWLISTS NOTHING. The suite has never been executed (see
# EXPECTED_SUITES), so there is no observed diagnostic anyone could claim is the
# harness's. Every diagnostic therefore fails the suite, which is the right
# default for a suite whose first run is still ahead of it.
#
# The file cannot simply be left pattern-less: GNU grep reads an EMPTY -f
# pattern file as matching every line, so an allowlist of only comments would
# filter out all diagnostics and silently disarm the whole check. The single
# pattern below is deliberately unmatchable — it is a placeholder that keeps the
# check armed, and the first entry with real evidence replaces it.
^COUNCIL_HAS_NO_KNOWN_HARNESS_DIAGNOSTICS_YET$
